{%- comment -%}
  AJ Story — the homepage teaser, on a real machine.

  THIS IS THE ONE PLACE AN IMAGE BEATS DRAWN CSS, and the reason is worth
  writing down because the opposite was true twice already.

  The About page could not use a photograph: the story is five hundred words,
  and a screen that is a fixed region of a raster cannot grow, so the copy
  either shrank or overflowed. A TEASER inverts that. Three short lines never
  need to reflow, so the fixed screen area costs nothing — and a photograph of
  a beige tower, a keyboard and a mouse sells 1997 far harder than a drawn
  bezel ever could.

  IT ALSO HAD TO BE FACE-ON. The first reference Alex sent was shot at a
  three-quarter angle, which would have meant a matrix3d transform to lay text
  on a trapezoid. This one is square to camera, so the overlay is a plain
  absolutely-positioned box.

  THE SCREEN COORDINATES ARE MEASURED, NOT EYEBALLED. The dark rectangle was
  found by scanning the PNG for near-black opaque pixels, restricted to the
  monitor's x-range so the drop shadow under the case could not stretch the
  bounds — a first pass without that restriction returned a square screen,
  which is not a shape any CRT was ever made in. The result reads 758x576px of
  2048, aspect 1.32, i.e. 4:3, which is the check that says the numbers are
  right.

  TYPE SCALES IN cqi, NOT px. The overlay is a percentage box over a fluid
  image, so a fixed font-size would overflow the glass the moment the image got
  narrow. Container query units tie the text to the image's own width, which is
  what makes this survive a phone without a single breakpoint.

  THE CTA IS NOT ON THE SCREEN. At any sensible size the glass is about 230px
  wide — fine for three lines of atmosphere, far too small for a tap target.
  The button sits below the machine, at a real size, as a real link.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign fallback = 'https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0731/4512/2918/files/retro_pc.H01.png?v=1785860292'
-%}

<div
  class="aj-story color-{{ s.color_scheme }}"
  style="padding-block-start: {{ s.padding-block-start }}px; padding-block-end: {{ s.padding-block-end }}px;"
  {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <div class="aj-story__inner">
    <div class="aj-story__machine" style="--aj-story-phosphor: {{ s.phosphor }};">
      {%- comment -%}
        Rendered through image_url/image_tag when the image is picked in the
        theme editor, because that is what produces a srcset and lets Shopify
        negotiate WebP — the source PNG is 1.8MB at 2048px and must never reach
        a phone at that weight. The hardcoded Files URL is only a fallback so
        the section is not blank before anyone opens the editor; it still gets
        a width parameter, which Shopify's CDN honours.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if s.image != blank -%}
        {{
          s.image
          | image_url: width: 1400
          | image_tag:
            widths: '400, 600, 800, 1100, 1400',
            sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 40rem, 92vw',
            alt: s.image_alt,
            class: 'aj-story__img',
            loading: 'lazy'
        }}
      {%- else -%}
        <img
          class="aj-story__img"
          src="{{ fallback }}&width=1400"
          srcset="{{ fallback }}&width=600 600w, {{ fallback }}&width=900 900w, {{ fallback }}&width=1400 1400w"
          sizes="(min-width: 750px) 40rem, 92vw"
          alt="{{ s.image_alt | escape }}"
          width="2048"
          height="2048"
          loading="lazy"
        >
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Decorative: the story is in the link below, and a screen reader
        spelling out an ASCII prompt before it is noise rather than atmosphere.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if s.screen_lines != blank -%}
        <div class="aj-story__crt" aria-hidden="true">
          {%- assign lines = s.screen_lines | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
          {%- for line in lines -%}
            {%- assign trimmed = line | strip -%}
            {%- if trimmed != blank -%}
              <p class="aj-story__line">{{ trimmed | escape }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
          <p class="aj-story__line aj-story__line--cursor"><span></span></p>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="aj-story__copy">
      {%- if s.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="aj-story__eyebrow">{{ s.eyebrow | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if s.teaser != blank -%}
        <p class="aj-story__teaser">{{ s.teaser | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if s.cta_text != blank -%}
        <a class="aj-story__cta" href="{{ s.cta_link | default: '/pages/about-us' }}">
          {{- s.cta_text | escape -}}
          <span class="aj-story__caret" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  /*
    STACKED ON A PHONE, SIDE BY SIDE FROM 750px.

    The machine is a wide object and the copy is three short lines, so stacking
    them on a desktop left a column of dead space either side and pushed the
    button most of a screen below the image it belongs to. Horizontal puts the
    CTA level with the monitor, which is where the eye already is.

    Mobile keeps the stack — two 45%-wide columns on a phone would be a small
    picture next to a narrow ribbon of text — but everything tightens.
  */
  .aj-story__inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    max-width: 58rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: 1.25rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-story__inner {
      flex-direction: row;
      gap: 3rem;
      text-align: left;
    }

    /* min-width: 0 so the image column can actually shrink — a flex item
       defaults to min-width: auto and would refuse to go below its content
       width, forcing the copy column into a sliver. */
    .aj-story__machine {
      flex: 1 1 54%;
      min-width: 0;
    }

    .aj-story__copy {
      flex: 1 1 46%;
    }
  }

  /* Capped on a phone so the machine does not eat the fold on its own. */
  .aj-story__machine {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 24rem;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-story__machine {
      max-width: none;
    }
  }

  .aj-story__eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--aj-price-act, #7a3fa0);
  }

  /* The container the overlay measures itself against. Without this the cqi
     units below have nothing to resolve to and the text falls back to being
     far too large. */
  .aj-story__machine {
    container-type: inline-size;
    position: relative;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .aj-story__img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  /*
    Measured off the PNG, not estimated. See the note at the top of the file:
    x 311-1069, y 604-1180 of 2048, which is 4:3 and therefore believable.
  */
  .aj-story__crt {
    position: absolute;
    left: 15.19%;
    top: 29.49%;
    width: 37.01%;
    height: 28.12%;

    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.4cqi;
    padding: 0 2cqi;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-align: left;

    /* The glass is flat grey in the render, so the phosphor bloom and the
       scanlines are added here — otherwise the text looks pasted on rather
       than emitted. */
    background:
      radial-gradient(
        ellipse at 50% 55%,
        color-mix(in srgb, var(--aj-story-phosphor) 12%, transparent) 0%,
        transparent 70%
      ),
      repeating-linear-gradient(
        to bottom,
        rgb(255 255 255 / 0.045) 0 1px,
        transparent 1px 3px
      );
  }

  .aj-story__line {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);

    /* cqi, so the type tracks the image's width. A px size would overflow the
       glass the moment the image narrowed. */
    font-size: 2.15cqi;
    line-height: 1.5;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--aj-story-phosphor, #5cf08a);
    text-shadow: 0 0 1.4cqi color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 55%, transparent);
  }

  .aj-story__line--cursor span {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 1.4cqi;
    height: 2.2cqi;
    background: var(--aj-story-phosphor, #5cf08a);
    box-shadow: 0 0 1.4cqi color-mix(in srgb, var(--aj-story-phosphor, #5cf08a) 55%, transparent);
    animation: aj-story-blink 1.1s steps(1, end) infinite;
  }

  @keyframes aj-story-blink {
    50% {
      opacity: 0;
    }
  }

  .aj-story__teaser {
    max-width: 34ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-story__teaser {
      margin-inline: 0;
      font-size: 1.25rem;
    }
  }

  .aj-story__cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block-start: 1.1rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.35rem;
    border-radius: var(--aj-tile-radius, 8px);
    background: var(--aj-price-act, #7a3fa0);
    color: #ffffff;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: opacity 0.15s ease;
  }

  @media (hover: hover) {
    .aj-story__cta:hover {
      opacity: 0.88;
    }

    .aj-story__cta:hover .aj-story__caret {
      transform: translateX(3px);
    }
  }

  /* Nudges on hover, never on a loop: motion that answers an action. */
  .aj-story__caret {
    transition: transform 0.15s ease;
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    /* One notch larger relative to the image, because at phone width the glass
       is only ~120px across and 2.15cqi lands under 8px. */
    .aj-story__line {
      font-size: 2.6cqi;
    }

    .aj-story__inner {
      gap: 0.75rem;
      padding-inline: 1rem;
    }

    .aj-story__teaser {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .aj-story__cta {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      width: 100%;
      margin-block-start: 0.9rem;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .aj-story__line--cursor span,
    .aj-story__caret {
      animation: none;
      transition: none;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "AJ Story",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Homepage teaser. The full story lives on the About page — this one is atmosphere plus a link, and should stay short."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Our story" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "The machine" },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "Computer image",
      "info": "Must be face-on with the screen square to camera. Falls back to the uploaded retro PC if empty. Picking it here lets Shopify serve resized WebP instead of the 1.8MB PNG."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "image_alt", "label": "Image alt text", "default": "A beige 1990s desktop computer" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "screen_lines",
      "label": "Text on the screen",
      "info": "One line each, uppercased automatically. Three lines maximum — the glass is small and a cursor is added after them.",
      "default": "C:\\> WHOAREWE.EXE\nTwo guys.\nOne deal a day."
    },
    { "type": "color", "id": "phosphor", "label": "Phosphor", "default": "#5cf08a" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Below the machine" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "teaser",
      "label": "Teaser line",
      "default": "We missed the dot-com boom by a decade. So we started this instead."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_text", "label": "Button", "default": "Read our story" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "cta_link", "label": "Button link" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Appearance" },
    { "type": "color_scheme", "id": "color_scheme", "label": "Color scheme", "default": "scheme-1" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Padding" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-start", "label": "Top", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 40 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-end", "label": "Bottom", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 60 }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "AJ Story" }]
}
{% endschema %}
